{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Fastest_and_Less_trigonometry_required)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Fastest and Less trigonometry required)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4(FAST)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4(FAST)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Law_of_Sines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Law of Sines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de79c06af394e175458e0742a6f7114168a4767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/510d81cec281a452485174a4373a1ef5e3ed5534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot BD=CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d4c500222f31337d7b0597d15b5a15e3bfe6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB=15^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf82288a7fbd825f1b95a4fc1c7aeaa9c49f364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB.$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d3aa0516676972677ff486236770c64237326a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }54^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(B) }60^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(C) }72^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(D) }75^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(E) }90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"416\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Fastest_and_Less_trigonometry_required.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Fastest_and_Less_trigonometry_required)\">Solution 1 (Fastest and Less trigonometry required)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Fastest and Less trigonometry required)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>No good diagram is actually needed for this problem if you are fluent in a geometrical sense.\n</p><p>Drop the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/0809976a25e44457494bccf7b15d5435a5e8ce51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/5432278922264e17d111671c8816b919bb36bc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = 1+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e4d8979ad9680b15b7f9be746300c26081eaa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 1, DC = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> WLOG. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is 45-45-90 and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18e5c209bf1457e8ee231aeb910dc327066f19d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA = 1+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Recall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/0809976a25e44457494bccf7b15d5435a5e8ce51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. But, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291a26605884e355c23c524c392c07ad49e5df5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEA$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is a 30-60-90 triangle hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e0246aa7924995722919add45f187ea031e8f649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3} a = EA = 1+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f73435cb74734092eb5c1dbd56c10c2bdc8e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(\\sqrt{3}-1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a9ed4c7781a9ab3b3106efdd1f3e21c9b6b5b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60059bfc167295da691f7c8bb03d66c1d38f1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 2 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{2} = \\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/6150604c0e17e7a669394e3dfa86a5bac2c5217a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}+3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />. Then, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21a24b107040c657e846a3c03c69de67147a5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c293a82f985d3d996342342fd2987fc35cbce9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\theta) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}+3}{3-\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{12+6\\sqrt{3}}{6} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p><b>Ending 1: Memorization:</b>, tangent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/dedd77d029c19ec5ed32b0f5b1275ad02b22b1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d2c7ef186745cbfcaa694d1ea7749a2277a395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917175428fd186c0e68e654eab2d9a9e6afb0d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{75^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><b>Ending 2: Double Angle Identity + Tangential Solve)</b> By double angle identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698df18f478bdeb7f438957db9c9625330aa84e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(2\\theta) = \\frac{2\\tan(\\theta)}{1-\\tan^2(\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"177\" height=\"45\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0eee1261304602643677e5056f3a3fd313b3f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta) = 2+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"24\" /> we have that firstly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400b88df36fd8104d7c07bdba243627593ee7288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\in (0,90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, since it is positive and is part of a triangle, and when solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb7f4d0445db8d66f9859cfe661a232801bb8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(2\\theta) = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\ : \\ 2\\theta \\in (90,180)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"261\" height=\"43\" />. Recall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b387ba001b821f740f5141198a1a8c0ddf4450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(150^\\circ) = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8caebb4a8c6e06d76b9886e6fa7c8afb550c2e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(150^\\circ) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/0157966f64ea9145148df7687457bfb16034ac75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(150^\\circ) = \\frac{\\sin(150^\\circ)}{\\cos(150^\\circ)} = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"245\" height=\"45\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148c10bf0314cd3496e35f0b9b181d0505292467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\theta = 150^\\circ \\implies \\theta = \\boxed{75^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"199\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw a good diagram! Now, let's call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d5c2028d4fea4892610e737d0746b1a474e1169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=t$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261792cf28433aa9856ebf3958c863f0bd0376e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=2t$\" width=\"69\" height=\"12\" />. Given the rather nice angles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/33053d88a516dd3b2803c9b60cae855eae9472d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b6c980833711545ef47dcbe863304ddd0866cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> as you can see, let's do trig. Drop an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />; call this point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. We realize that there is no specific factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> we can call this just yet, so let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d69519ed806e6c8bdc87b9999e08e90fa7f35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=kt$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e16240b304adbc6a609e273a0ecce86090cb880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABH}$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228fc4cbd62f920ae803c6998e25c16319c1b60b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH=kt$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" />. Using the 60-degree angle in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1771453cd8678fe3976e89c602d121285a7b9bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADH}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa0dc51357415c4624f2f6b889243a2992c361af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DH=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}kt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"43\" />. The comparable ratio is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6800963fb7f9e55628f737df60c02e53a8113f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH-DH=t$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />. If we involve our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d654d48690edd85b4ce6fb4512f5eac1125043d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kt(\\frac{3}{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"41\" />. Eliminating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> and removing radicals from the denominator, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ad83ce1b43a52c1321f80ef049747b36a0883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />. From there, one can easily obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8bfa3641fe702c831265cfe89f6e0880ecabca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC=3t-kt=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{2}t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"199\" height=\"41\" />. Now we finally have a desired ratio. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/42556614bb5a2dc60edbfe4c84f848e8a6edbdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\angle ACH = 2+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" /> upon calculation, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2365f9b3e83e4bb7980e961b338159c1f3929261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACH$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> can be simplified. Indeed, if you know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/452dd327f74eab1eee390cae27d2734efb367edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(75)=2+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" /> or even take a minute or two to work out the sine and cosine using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fa794faee5eca4511a0008fa73dbdf9f62ad0ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)^2+\\cos(x)^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />, and perhaps the half- or double-angle formulas, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917175428fd186c0e68e654eab2d9a9e6afb0d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{75^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17586f266d8a614e45964038dbd11de47c7389e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae496febaf2b1761c7c6d022bae1848b056d12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 2$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. As above, we are able to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b6c980833711545ef47dcbe863304ddd0866cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc36f0bd7226b903e00c756fe5482c7f0550b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Using Law of Sines on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/8810a26f59e2c67b5f2ff052a7e2a294fef0a03e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7db8d87d60d2e28f371c9a9e52f476feacacda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{\\sin15^\\circ} = \\frac{AD}{\\sin 45^\\circ} = \\frac{AB}{\\sin 120^\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"38\" /> Since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2944536765e5bb51c35025d8b1191d09b22d17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 15^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c13accd1ec6e8e89383fc8db6a20558a1c08a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f591fe1a17afa8a8b373f3c01571ee6ba09a5493.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 120^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"41\" /> we can compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/4391e5a5c202b1debdfd9c62b87ebff4eb614560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e1edc7499ff4389fe03113c794ec29838261c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we apply Law of Cosines to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/0264d4807b205cf689b34463e5162a17f6019ce7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = (1+\\sqrt{3})^2 + 2^2 - (2)(1+\\sqrt{3})(2)(\\cos 60^\\circ).\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"21\" /> Simplifying the right side, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/8445301c82a6031e86d058cc5234280367eb374b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6949d063abaa5a92c940ccfcd05139ddea42966f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we apply Law of Sines to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74ebe6bdaf4a21a719f89b7ca663cda568e59951.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{\\sin 45^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{2}}{\\sin ACB}.\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"44\" /> After rearranging and noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da5d34083101299ac719670817c6aeee9229e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6bb025c555e03b755f3052947c3b0a90fab3aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin ACB = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}+3\\sqrt{2}}{4\\sqrt{3}}.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Dividing the right side by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c3241b8524bf243107dd1202e3be940c05d38409.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin ACB = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"41\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0728bebb477a2636300c56851b6a6f9e382c1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/dedd77d029c19ec5ed32b0f5b1275ad02b22b1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd79ddaf1f259c44cdbdf9906325f9c8f8d0e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd79ddaf1f259c44cdbdf9906325f9c8f8d0e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> is not a choice, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63dba1064b7095376b7e5b0de4097e75c0bcef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = \\boxed{75^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>Note that we can also confirm that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b7fb32ab3949dcbf7943bb0df015eab0fba02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB \\neq 105^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /> by computing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> with Law of Sines.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4.28FAST.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4(FAST)\">Solution 4(FAST)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4(FAST)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1da91c03d9dd2044be09d7667e93ab002456541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADB} = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e496fc0f919270907eb896fd02e1b19bb9276279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADC} = 60$\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" />. Seeing these angles makes us think of 30-60-90 triangles. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eebdf149af4e61db413dd0c4993aa24ed775b7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAE} = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88ba146220d6c86b3de381a9ad516d72e5d5d4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAE} = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a108f6ba58046a281a287b27cf06d9ade6c1b69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/1811b88741d9c178a49642bf03d85594ebe75f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b21dcf758bec5a89fef106dea55bf37816b1e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = y\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"23\" /> and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463d2f272d5bf52ebdd2a23f01b463cb78c2aa38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b55ae7540e55a73ca1d056abc67a8111f2fcc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = y\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"23\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/1500422ffec26c6d714e3d53ce9257723b2ce292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{x(\\sqrt{3} + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"43\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf0c7c0d1112bf098b2d0a300c5a2f6d3c9d929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\frac{4x - x(\\sqrt{3} + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"43\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce28a0f3b5cc66450e7a26ca230790d402f7e135.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\angle{ACE}} = \\frac{AE}{CE} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"39\" />. Looking that the answer options we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e623d9c9267b9ef6002fbf19ed676306d7a5f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{75^\\circ} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />. This means the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n~coolmath_2018 6 7\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Law_of_Sines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Law_of_Sines)\">Solution 5 (Law of Sines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Law of Sines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc36f0bd7226b903e00c756fe5482c7f0550b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b6c980833711545ef47dcbe863304ddd0866cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3def246d7b92540694cddd1c554e34b4b2cc6bef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB = 15^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/7380868ca9231086c231adbfca7a37d1c9dc86dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = \\theta$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21f1e805bc51c3bfce35e7d10ec145142358154a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC = 120^\\circ - \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f8ac0334f44e57a38fcb714ae312a128280781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta)} = \\frac{AD}{\\sin \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"171\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825f880cb222ec2cc60fd40996c91d26ce9bf329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\space$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99ae76d8601c1e379e11fbb2b3ad7b648b67bc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BD}{\\sin15^\\circ} = \\frac{AD}{\\sin45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee7806ec5c5bdc9d55b46e36203fabc1544c0022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BD}{CD} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta)}{\\sin15^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\sin45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"235\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42607b9c80e120b823fad4442efac16a9efcaf0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta)}{\\sin15^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\sin45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"214\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>By the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Trigonometric_identities#Triple-angle_identities\">Triple-angle Identities</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e586014a1919f84171e0dcb911904e55a484f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 45^\\circ = 3\\sin15^\\circ -4\\sin^3 15^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"233\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a092fa3ae33a40652f24d2a31963877c77647b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta)}{2} = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{3\\ -4\\sin^2 15^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cfd8851de8effae3a2592d2d3dfaa2cd58d5e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 15^\\circ = \\frac{1 - \\cos 30^\\circ}{2} = \\frac{1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{2} = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"338\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b704547dcf3d1cfc065352c8aa875d6f6d9d9faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta)}{2} = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{3 - 4 \\cdot \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{3}}{4}} = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{1+\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"312\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574c2535e849618de007dfa12122ed22ca19d3a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta)} = \\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"192\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b03b291a3dd6d92e8d5510db7b7235634275e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(120^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin120^\\circ \\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta \\cos120^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\cos\\theta + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sin\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"535\" height=\"43\" />，so \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf4716d8237f42403142d8a6f69734d5999b6e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\cos\\theta + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sin\\theta} = \\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"241\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f6fd5df87b352c54dbd3eb8ee527d08e7d478a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\cos\\theta + \\sin\\theta}{2 \\sin \\theta} = \\frac{2}{1+\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"220\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b81ef31c7b046efb1ad0c81571a1a8c74b0d410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\cot \\theta = \\frac{2}{1+\\sqrt{3}} - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2 + 2 \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"291\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a709934a2d18e4dd6ada2df6bc543d663769264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot \\theta = \\frac{\\cos \\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"187\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13e2ffe62a298decb49f15f5114e127a6355f2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = k(\\sqrt{3} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"24\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a669a152f503f1dd7a11c51d468e3cc04f290341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = k(\\sqrt{3} + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a5786b65663e55e2330a47ecf32b4d8666d9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5837c4188aed34253edfe24b2cdfad79064ca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2(\\sqrt{3} + 1)^2 + k^2(\\sqrt{3} - 1)^2 = 8k^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6953124f326c13769fdea459d2ec30bbbc5a68cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"73\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12556b0c2e278695708ff9884f403be645290d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"120\" height=\"48\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d025068f006c754a786cffb0605cd184b030ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"122\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5cae76a5400e21e6afc8ecd50ded6f54807595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 2 \\theta = 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{2 \\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2 \\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"261\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c216bbf32b7328689a643d28e01a3416a66feba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\theta$\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd96fce8011b053b9d83a5b2d39ec3c756f0f66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. However we can rule out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/976fae0f74c2e6402fa9cedcb86a0fb9843024c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 15^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is negative.\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64ca77c4bd244747d7089698c9a3a28476cc3b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\theta = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c083d522261d5925cfa617b047bc519c1eb053e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 75^\\circ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For starters, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5ddb7f065dcbbb965048f16c98b10e6a43ef58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD=120^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" /> Dropping perpendiculars <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/42236f28c5e526dc4471f83f8fb1768aa6003d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DX}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e730a98f5c74d99ad253902ba164219e8a9234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CY}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7afd4b86ac3ea6ad04d467469c2efbfec8aeb41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADX=120^\\circ-45^\\circ=75^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a9db2dee8c88673e3843ff5691c4f39ed3c07a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDX=45^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75069193aac5943aac9b2fb68d912fe1841ace81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23b358cd3c8f5f18c6d70169315f64d75d3617e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=2.$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" /> This tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c409a4ec87d5ab203ac671784d83c9cceedabfbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX=DX=\\sqrt{2}/2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"24\" /> Using trigonometric identities, we find that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f71d0de55892ea9d86dd9abecc258fb4098983d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\angle ADX=\\tan 75^\\circ=\\dfrac{\\sqrt 6+\\sqrt 2}{\\sqrt 6-\\sqrt 2}.\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"45\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/08213af06f8974cda1fbe67dd4fab1d232097633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX/DX=\\dfrac{\\sqrt 6+\\sqrt 2}{\\sqrt 6-\\sqrt 2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"176\" height=\"48\" /> which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/070beedfc3af02266373ae8b6da66344dbb1fd9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt 2+\\sqrt 6}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"43\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8ed5efb2ba2e3b5b1e149c065c404759057b00c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AX+BX=\\dfrac{3\\sqrt 2+\\sqrt 6}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"251\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5aaa394ce78cf744038b4fb2bcf5efcb66d0d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCY$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a21514afad8a91b620d24bafc22c1b2d723d989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CY=BY=\\dfrac{3\\sqrt 2}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"43\" /> Thus, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134e51bc51dc5e14749dd4b967b1a01b8decc4db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC]=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot CY=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot \\dfrac{3\\sqrt 2+\\sqrt 6}{2}\\cdot \\dfrac{3\\sqrt 2}{2}=\\dfrac{9+3\\sqrt 3}{4}.\\]\" width=\"452\" height=\"41\" />\nAdditionally, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22ad2cd336c9a41960f6046cb44d83fd9a2fae7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AY=AB-BY=\\sqrt{6}/2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"24\" /> Applying the Pythagorean Theorem to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782f0a677df99bdb1ed78f93fd4d8b834fc07214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AYC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> then tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47128f5c653e59acbb1e43b16965aac9b320593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\sqrt{6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"21\" /> By the trigonometric formula for area,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9c5a16e23dd3476c2c83079bfe7fa64beae848d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC]=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AC\\cdot \\sin \\angle ACB=\\dfrac{3\\sqrt 6}{2}\\sin \\angle ACB.\\]\" width=\"414\" height=\"41\" />\nSetting this equal to our other area and solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d47785e76488c14975cbac050fdb17bf818227f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\angle ACB=\\dfrac{\\sqrt 6+\\sqrt 2}{4},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"43\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a7a06901c9b49455be23f09736a9c69191f4bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB=\\boxed{75^\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"124\" height=\"26\" /> ~vaporwave\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194858\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.077 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.098 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 948/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 32319/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.577      1 -total\n 60.41%    8.202      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.13%    5.041      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7860:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194858 and revision id 293415. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}